ith</surname><given-names>RA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Benefit of mammography screening in women ages 40 to 49 years. Current evidence from randomized controlled trials</article-title><source>Cancer</source><year>1995</year><volume>75</volume><fpage>1619</fpage><lpage>1626</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Cancer||75|1619||bib29|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8826919</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib30"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Tyndel</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Austoker</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Henderson</surname><given-names>BJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Brain</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Bankhead</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Clements</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Watson</surname><given-names>EK</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>What is the psychological impact of mammographic screening on younger women with a family history of breast cancer? Findings from a prospective cohort study by the PIMMS Management Group</article-title><source>J Clin Oncol</source><year>2007</year><volume>25</volume><fpage>3823</fpage><lpage>3830</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'J Clin Oncol||25|3823||bib30|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17761970</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib31"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Watson</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Duvivier</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name><name><surname>Wade-Walsh</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Ashley</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Davidson</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Papaikonomou</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Murday</surname><given-names>V</given-names>